      {
        "id": "u1",
        "kind": "CONCEPT",
        "label": "Definition, Principles, and Requirements of Vapour Phase Refining",
        "attributes": {
          "depth": "explanation"
        },
        "subtopic_ids": [
          "s1"
        ],
        "rationale": "Defines vapour phase refining and explains the two-step mechanism as well as key conditions necessary for the process to work.",
        "review_flags": [],
        "contextualization": {
          "value": "none",
          "evidence": []
        },
        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "p1",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "heading"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "# Vapour Phase Refining",
            "start": 0,
            "end": 23
          },
          {
            "id": "p2",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "heading"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "## What is it?",
            "start": 25,
            "end": 39
          },
          {
            "id": "p3",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "explanation"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "**Vapour Phase Refining** is a method used to purify metals by converting them into a **volatile compound**, which is then decomposed to give back the **pure metal**. This technique is used when a metal has impurities that are difficult to remove by other methods like electrolytic refining.",
            "start": 41,
            "end": 332
          },
          {
            "id": "p4",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "heading"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "## Basic Principle",
            "start": 334,
            "end": 352
          },
          {
            "id": "p5",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "The method works on a simple two-step idea:",
            "start": 354,
            "end": 397
          },
          {
            "id": "p6",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "explanation"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "1. **Step 1:** The impure metal is converted into a **volatile compound** (a compound that easily vaporizes) by reacting it with a suitable substance.",
            "start": 399,
            "end": 549
          },
          {
            "id": "p7",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "explanation"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "2. **Step 2:** This volatile compound is then **decomposed** (usually by heating) to give the **pure metal**.",
            "start": 550,
            "end": 659
          },
          {
            "id": "p8",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "heading"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "### Key Requirements:",
            "start": 661,
            "end": 682
          },
          {
            "id": "p9",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "- The volatile compound must be **easy to form** from the impure metal.",
            "start": 683,
            "end": 754
          },
          {
            "id": "p10",
            "category": "CONCEPT",
            "attributes": {
              "depth": "statement"
            },
            "formats": [
              "list"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "- The compound must be **easily decomposable** to give the pure metal back.",
            "start": 755,
            "end": 830
          },
          {
            "id": "p11",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "separator"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "---",
            "start": 832,
            "end": 835
          }
        ],
        "accuracy": {
          "verdict": "accurate",
          "reason": "The definition, two-step principle, and fundamental requirements for vapour phase refining are scientifically sound and standard.",
          "errors": []
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "u2",
        "kind": "EXAMPLE",
        "label": "Mond's Process for Nickel Refining",
        "attributes": {
          "context": "real_world",
          "treatment": "illustrative"
        },
        "subtopic_ids": [
          "s2"
        ],
        "rationale": "Illustrates the application of vapour phase refining to the purification of nickel using carbon monoxide.",
        "review_flags": [],
        "contextualization": {
          "value": "none",
          "evidence": []
        },
        "passages": [
          {
            "id": "p12",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "heading"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "## Important Examples",
            "start": 837,
            "end": 858
          },
          {
            "id": "p13",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "heading"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "### 1. **Mond's Process (for Nickel)**",
            "start": 860,
            "end": 898
          },
          {
            "id": "p14",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "Used to refine impure nickel.",
            "start": 900,
            "end": 929
          },
          {
            "id": "p15",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "**Step 1:** Impure nickel is heated in a stream of **carbon monoxide (CO)** gas at about 330–350 K. This forms a volatile compound called **nickel tetracarbonyl**.",
            "start": 931,
            "end": 1094
          },
          {
            "id": "p16",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "equation"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "$$Ni + 4CO \\xrightarrow{330-350K} Ni(CO)_4$$",
            "start": 1096,
            "end": 1140
          },
          {
            "id": "p17",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "prose"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "**Step 2:** The nickel tetracarbonyl vapor is then heated to a higher temperature (450–470 K), where it **decomposes** to give pure nickel and releases CO gas (which can be reused).",
            "start": 1142,
            "end": 1323
          },
          {
            "id": "p18",
            "category": "EXAMPLE",
            "attributes": {},
            "formats": [
              "equation"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "$$Ni(CO)_4 \\xrightarrow{450-470K} Ni \\text{ (pure)} + 4CO$$",
            "start": 1325,
            "end": 1384
          },
          {
            "id": "p19",
            "category": "ORGANIZATION",
            "attributes": {
              "subtype": "structural"
            },
            "formats": [
              "separator"
            ],
            "review_flags": [],
            "text": "---",
            "start": 1386,
            "end": 1389
          }
        ],
        "accuracy": {
          "verdict": "accurate",
          "reason": "The reaction temperatures (330–350 K for formation and 450–470 K for decomposition) and chemical equations for nickel tetracarbonyl formation and breakdown are completely accurate.",
          "errors": []
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "u3",
        "kind": "EXAMPLE",
        "label": "Van Arkel Method for Zirconium and Titanium",
        "attributes": {
          "context": "real_world",
          "treatment": "illustrative"
        },
        "subtopic_ids": [
          "s3"
        ],
        "rationale": "Illustrates vapour phase refining using iodine to purify zirconium or titanium on a heated tungsten filament.",
        "review_flags": [],
        "contextualization": {
